# tekacs/codex commit 9ffcf8db9078eae43d4111ff94259795c1e962c9 ("wake model when background exec commands complete")
# Source: https://github.com/tekacs/codex/commit/9ffcf8db9078eae43d4111ff94259795c1e962c9
# Parent in fork: ba573b4. The fork base is NOT current upstream main; e.g. Session::inject_or_start and
# handle_resource_update exist in the fork but not in upstream 33a0f766a6.
#
# NOTE: the codex-rs/models-manager/models.json hunk is omitted here (single-line JSON, ~50KB). Its only change:
# in gpt-5.5 base_instructions / instructions_template the sentence
#   "Do not end your turn while `exec_command` sessions needed for the user's request are still running."
# was replaced by
#   "If `exec_command` yields a live background process, treat it as background work: do not poll it, and end
#    your turn when there is no independent work left; the runtime completion notification will wake you."
# The rest of the patch follows verbatim.
#
From 9ffcf8db9078eae43d4111ff94259795c1e962c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Amar Sood (tekacs)" <pkg@tekacs.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 22:51:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wake model when background exec commands complete

- emit a pushed model input when a unified exec process completes after the original exec_command call yielded a live background process
- route completion input through the same active-or-idle pushed-input path used by RMCP resource updates, so active turns receive it and idle sessions wake
- suppress duplicate pushed completions when the original exec_command call already returned the terminal result inline
- update exec_command/write_stdin tool descriptions to tell the model to wait for runtime completion notifications instead of empty-polling unless it needs intermediate output or interaction
- cover active-turn pushed input delivery and unified exec process-state wake gating

Maintenance note: if upstream ever fixes this, this custom patch may be elided while rebasing onto upstream, but only after strict verification that upstream behavior is fully equivalent to this patch. Equivalence means background unified exec completions wake idle sessions, are delivered to active turns via the pushed-input path, do not duplicate inline exec_command results, and keep model-facing tool guidance aligned with that behavior.
